{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123772-gravity-and-forces","id":1123772,"title":"Gravity and Forces","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-01T22:39:39-07:00","id":1123772,"title":"Gravity and Forces","content":"Maybe it's just my reading, but Embracing the Earth Mother (2E page 299) seems to indicate that you can't control gravity until at least Forces 4, even when targeting an individual That has always seemed odd to me. But it has occurred to me that complete control over gravity's effect on objects with Forces 2 would allow powerful Prime-free telekinesis quite early, simply by redirecting gravity. But I don't like the idea that you can't do anything with Gravity at Forces 2 or 3. Uses I would find acceptable:<br /> <br /> -Reducing or increasing gravity's effect on an object up to 50%. This would go for both static or airborne targets.<br /> -Manipulating balance, to the point where you could, say, run across the top of a fence with no difficulty.<br /> -Redirecting the fall direction of an object by up to 45 degrees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T04:27:50-07:00","id":1123829,"title":"","content":"I would say you would first need a paradigm that acknowledges gravity as a force. That's pretty much going to be exclusive to those who buy in to this aspect of the Technocratic paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T05:56:32-07:00","id":1123847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123772-gravity-and-forces?p=1123829#post1123829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say you would first need a paradigm that acknowledges gravity as a force. That's pretty much going to be exclusive to those who buy in to this aspect of the Technocratic paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you mean a scientific paradigm. That's not exclusive to Technocrats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T06:36:29-07:00","id":1123854,"title":"","content":"Indeed, Aristotle already had theorized about this force. Of course, his ideas on the subject were a bit weird.<br /> <br /> But &quot;making things heavy&quot;, &quot;making things lighter&quot;, &quot;making things fall upwards&quot; have a place in mytology and fantasi, even when it's not necesarily interpreted as a tweaking a particular force. One way to deal with this is to interpret that mithical mages are tweaking gravity without calling it that way, but if we say that you need to believe in gravity to manipulate it, then mythic mages have right to ask to control with Force (and Force alone) any sort of bizarre mythological or fantasy &quot;forcelike stuff&quot;, including the transmutation of normal forces to of purely mythical or sci-fi &quot;forces&quot;. Actually, I'm ok with the latter idea, but the system seems geared for the former.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T10:12:34-07:00","id":1123915,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure things tending to fall down is part of everyone's paradigm, even where there is not formal understanding of it. I'm just saying that more than minor manipulations of it make sense as a MAJOR force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T11:14:56-07:00","id":1123947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123772-gravity-and-forces?p=1123915#post1123915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure things tending to fall down is part of everyone's paradigm, even where there is not formal understanding of it. I'm just saying that more than minor manipulations of it make sense as a MAJOR force.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really hard question. IRL things falling down is a part of every descriptive theory of the world because that is an objectively observable fact. But there's a major difference between &quot;things that have mass attract each other&quot; and Aristotelan &quot;things have down because they have more earth than fire in them&quot;. A mage who believes in Aristotelan physics and boards a Void Engineer ship to Pluto has to divide by zero because there is no &quot;down&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T11:29:44-07:00","id":1123955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mage who believes in Aristotelan physics and boards a Void Engineer ship to Pluto has to divide by zero because there is no &quot;down&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That opens an entirely different can of worms, because one could argue that for Aristotelian physics, &quot;down&quot; it's the direction where Earth is (as Earth was below the celestial dome of the universal engine where Spheres are, Pluto would be Sphere-ish and thus be &quot;above&quot; Earth).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-02-2017, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T12:02:10-07:00","id":1123962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123772-gravity-and-forces?p=1123854#post1123854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, Aristotle already had theorized about this force.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... well, I would definitely put him in the Order of Reason team <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123772-gravity-and-forces?p=1123915#post1123915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure things tending to fall down is part of everyone's paradigm, even where there is not formal understanding of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be true, but it is not that obvious to everyone. Exemple : You're on the top of a moving train with a ball in your hand. You throw the ball in the air. Where do the ball fall (ignore air resistance) ? You would be surprised to hear how many poeple think it will fall behind you... Gravity and movement are not that obvious concepts. Well, in my experience anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T13:06:18-07:00","id":1123986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I'm just saying that more than minor manipulations of it make sense as a MAJOR force.</span><br /> </span><br /> <br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, otherwise you could make someone to &quot;fall to the sky&quot; with just Forces 2 (change the direction of gravity's pull). Forces 2 it's powerful enough as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T13:06:30-07:00","id":1123987,"title":"","content":"Mage 1e divided forces into major and minor forces by type. Embracing the Earth Mother, which is on page 199 of my PDF edition of Mage 2e, looks like it was taken from the Mage 1e book.<br /> <br /> In Mage 1e, different forces required different types and gravity and nuclear forces required Forces 4 to manipulate and 5 to create. Mage 2e, revised and Mage 20 go with amount of force controlled. So, with Forces 2 if you are not using Mage 1e rules, you can do minor gravity effects.<br /> <br /> Embracing the Earth Mother's larger effects seem pretty powerful--if you raise someone's gravity by 5 Gs, they might even die from the crushing pressure. So, Embracing the Earth Mother probably stays at Forces 4 for the higher-level impact but you could do light kinetics at Forces 2 and 3.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T13:17:00-07:00","id":1123989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may be true, but it is not that obvious to everyone. Exemple : You're on the top of a moving train with a ball in your hand. You throw the ball in the air. Where do the ball fall (ignore air resistance) ? You would be surprised to hear how many poeple think it will fall behind you... Gravity and movement are not that obvious concepts. Well, in my experience anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>The formalization of gravity as a force may not be obvious, but the <i>applications </i>of gravity manipulation are widespread in all mysitic paradigms. For instance, when a monk levitates, when a witch fly with her broom, when a psychic uses telekinesis. Shouldn't these count as &quot;defying gravity&quot;?, if not, then what force should be used by these mystics? (I mean, flying propelled by hurricane level winds it's possible, but seems a bit uncomfortable and nothing like what telekinesis looks like)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-02-2017, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:15:36-07:00","id":1124029,"title":"","content":"I do believe that several Mystics (actually the large fraction that do not walk with science principles) would not consider gravity as a Force as defined in Physics. I really am not sure that the concepts of intensity, direction or reaction are used by those Mages. However, it can be considered as a force of will, a consequence of a light and serene soul, a consequence of element forces, etc. May be those beliefs are more considered by Eastern Traditions (not sure about that though, to be confirmed). I would need to think more about, but I think we can think of many causes to gravity without considering it as an Force.<br /> <br /> And yes, I wonder what the witch believes in when she flies her broom or what the Taftany Mage believes when he flies the carpet. I'm not sure they think about it as defying gravity or any law of Physics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T08:54:32-07:00","id":1124320,"title":"","content":"Probably they don't. Some magics may not have any logic (the broom works because <i>everyone </i>knows witches travel by broom), while others work on logics that are alien to our mindsets, like the idea that reality, including movement, weight, and the fact that we seem to be so attached to earth, it's all an illusion of the mind.<br /> <br /> However, we use Forces when we deal with these stuff,even when we speak of Paradigms that do not aknowledge ANY &quot;physical force&quot; from a conceptual point (otherwise, you have to accept that a buddhist can do litterally everything with Mind alone).<br /> <br /> The question related to the thread would be: Is <i>any of</i> <i>this </i>a manipulation of &quot;a major force&quot;? Because Forces made the division between minnor and major part of it's working. Actually, If my memory doesn't fail, M20 doesn't seem to have that distinction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T10:26:08-07:00","id":1124363,"title":"","content":"I do not think M20 distincts minor and major forces neither. It's all about area and amplitude increase (left to the ST judgement depending of the kind of chronicle, as always, which is ok with me).<br /> <br /> \u200bI understand your point <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> <br /> I might be mistaken, but the authors are Scientists with a capital S. I believe more and more that they wrote Mage (like Ars Magica) according to an Hermetic viewpoint. Therefore, I always differenciate the system from the background explanations. The buddhist of your exemple can believe he can do everything with his mind alone. This is not the same thing as doing everything with Mind alone (here the Mind Sphere). He would still use Forces. Spheres are not accepted by all Mages. They're just the common langage proposed by Hermetics to communicate when the Council of the Nine Traditions was created.<br /> <br /> The way the Sphere of Forces is described is largely understandable from a Scientific point of view. But that is the system. The buddhist will still use the Forces Sphere to use his magick. However, he strongly believes in the power of the mind. This is not incompatible.<br /> <br /> I actually go further. I do not use the Technocratic Spheres for that reason. I do not care about how the system defines the Spheres. I use the same system for every player. However, I demand them to justify their deeds according to their paradigms. Those do not need to be close to the Hermetic style. If a player tells me he wants his/her character to fly, I tell him/her to buy Forces and Mind dots. That said, the in-game reason for the character to fly is left to the player. The character can draw that power for gods, sacrifices for spirits, sheer will or meditation, that's up to him/her.<br /> <br /> When I hear the whole argument about &quot;yeah but technocratics spheres are more adapted to certain paradigms&quot;, I actually hear &quot;yeah but with the Technocratic Spheres I could do more with less XP&quot;. It falls into powergaming and I do not allow it in my sessions if the result is not believable from a role-play point of view ^^ That is my sole opinion though.<br /> <br /> (I think I digressed a little here... well sorry ^^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T16:41:00-07:00","id":1124529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123772-gravity-and-forces?p=1124363#post1124363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually go further. I do not use the Technocratic Spheres for that reason. I do not care about how the system defines the Spheres. I use the same system for every player. However, I demand them to justify their deeds according to their paradigms. Those do not need to be close to the Hermetic style. If a player tells me he wants his/her character to fly, I tell him/her to buy Forces and Mind dots. That said, the in-game reason for the character to fly is left to the player. The character can draw that power for gods, sacrifices for spirits, sheer will or meditation, that's up to him/her.<br /> <br /> When I hear the whole argument about &quot;yeah but technocratics spheres are more adapted to certain paradigms&quot;, I actually hear &quot;yeah but with the Technocratic Spheres I could do more with less XP&quot;. It falls into powergaming and I do not allow it in my sessions if the result is not believable from a role-play point of view ^^ That is my sole opinion though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Were it me, I would just fold any particular functions of the Technocratic Spheres into their regular counterparts, and make it up to the individual player to determine if their character can use them. With Data, for example, all you're really getting is 1) a limitation pertaining to the powers being tied to the Grid, and 2) a different table for establishing connections. The former is entirely replicated by having the user's Focus limit their magick, and the latter can just be used as an alternate to the regular Correspondence chart, for those characters who use information rather than Sympathetic Magic. We don't need an entire write-up for this.<br /> <br /> Same with Primal Utility. If the character believes that the value humans traffic in is a source of Quintessence, let them use Prime to manipulate it. Etc, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:25:00-07:00","id":1124583,"title":"","content":"People seem to forget a lot that although mystic paradigms have roots in the past, most practitioners have a modern frame of reference. Really basic stuff like gravity would probably be incorporated into modern mystics' paradigms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 08-04-2017, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T23:22:47-07:00","id":1124634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123772-gravity-and-forces?p=1124583#post1124583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People seem to forget a lot that although mystic paradigms have roots in the past, most practitioners have a modern frame of reference. Really basic stuff like gravity would probably be incorporated into modern mystics' paradigms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This, pretty much.<br /> *unless* the mystic paradigm in question that is being practiced actively *disagrees* with a specific part of the scientific paradigm, I think it can be quite safely presumed that the mystic will simply use what they learned in school and 'common knowledge' to explain it, these days.<br /> <br /> Or put differently, just because you are a shaman dreamspeaker doesn't mean that your lore and teachings explain gravity (And just because you are a shaman doesn't mean that you have the same paradigm as all other shaman groups,either..some of which might explain gravity with spirits or world creation lore..). So you go with Newton on that thing. Unless another mystic has an explanation that actually fits your paradigm and that you actually like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T03:00:33-07:00","id":1125152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123772-gravity-and-forces?p=1124583#post1124583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People seem to forget a lot that although mystic paradigms have roots in the past, most practitioners have a modern frame of reference. Really basic stuff like gravity would probably be incorporated into modern mystics' paradigms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Technocratic conditioning via education is quite strong regardless. My concept personally believes that her Chaos Magick would somehow be scientifically explicable in the future, she doesn't think it is &quot;beyond scientific reason&quot;. It's rather telling that she embraces the Technocratic paradigm on some basic level despite not using it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T15:33:57-07:00","id":1125710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123772-gravity-and-forces?p=1123987#post1123987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Mage 2e, revised and Mage 20 go with amount of force controlled. So, with Forces 2 if you are not using Mage 1e rules, you can do minor gravity effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly. Reversing the gravity on a tennis ball would be force 2, while manipulating the gravity of a whole room would be 4.<br /> Page 516 of M20 specifies that Forces 4 is reserved to &quot;control major forces&quot;, in the sense of appliying previous Force effects to a larger scale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123772-gravity-and-forces?p=1123989#post1123989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The formalization of gravity as a force may not be obvious, but the <i>applications </i>of gravity manipulation are widespread in all mysitic paradigms.</div> </div> </div> </div>That aside, we're in the 21th century now, and the idea of gravity as a force has been around for a few centuries. You just don't need to have to know gravity equations to understand that there is a force keeping you on the earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}